.TH tkubase64 n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkubase64
.PP
Base64 encode/decode panel. Built on \fBtclutils::tubase64\fR. An input area, an output area, and Encode/Decode buttons. The panel holds text: Encode converts it to UTF\-8 first, Decode reads the bytes as UTF\-8, so \fBJörg €\fR becomes \fBSsO2cmcg4oKs\fR and comes back unchanged (0.2).
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkubase64::widget .w ?-width N? ?-height N?]
::tkutils::tkubase64::setInput  $w text
::tkutils::tkubase64::encode    $w        ;# input -> Base64, returns output
::tkutils::tkubase64::decode    $w        ;# input -> plain, returns output
::tkutils::tkubase64::getInput  $w
::tkutils::tkubase64::getOutput $w
.CE
.SS Launcher
.CS
tclsh bin/tkubase64.tcl
.CE
